1
00:00:00,630 --> 00:00:03,950
I wore it for you, Caleb. Like I promised.

2
00:00:05,235 --> 00:00:06,435
Keep walking, ma'am.

3
00:00:10,708 --> 00:00:12,905
Her name was Rose Calloway.

4
00:00:13,216 --> 00:00:15,010
She was twenty-four, from St.

5
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:20,548
Louis, and she had never seen the face
of the man she had come a thousand miles

6
00:00:20,588 --> 00:00:21,473
to marry.

7
00:00:35,152 --> 00:00:36,772
What's in the box, Mr. Pruitt?

8
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,920
Trouble, miss. The kind that
has to reach the marshal.

9
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:52,877
When I say jump, girl, you jump!

10
00:00:52,917 --> 00:00:57,977
Don't let Crane have it.
Whatever they tell you.

11
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:20,650
She went up the mountain! Find her!

12
00:01:21,336 --> 00:01:25,917
She hid until dark between two
boulders, in her mother's wedding dress,

13
00:01:25,957 --> 00:01:31,764
holding a box she could not open, while
men with guns searched the rocks below.

14
00:01:32,168 --> 00:01:37,012
In three days, her own groom would
walk her down Main Street in handcuffs.

15
00:01:37,253 --> 00:01:42,283
But the strangest part of this story is
not how she ended up on that mountain.

16
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:45,104
It's what she was holding.

17
00:01:50,283 --> 00:01:53,863
She jumped with the box,
boss. Went up the rocks.

18
00:01:55,037 --> 00:01:58,737
Then find her. Mountains
are full of sad accidents.

19
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:09,519
Silas Crane was the most
respected man in Cedar Bluff.

20
00:02:09,922 --> 00:02:13,106
He sat in the front pew of
the church he had paid for.

21
00:02:13,347 --> 00:02:17,797
For two years the gold stage
had been robbed on Raven Pass.

22
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,885
Nobody had ever suspected him.

23
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:29,560
Miss Calloway. Welcome
to Cedar Bluff, ma'am.

24
00:02:30,548 --> 00:02:33,648
Son, she's marrying you, not that mirror.

25
00:02:34,605 --> 00:02:39,185
Twenty-six letters, Abel. I know
her better than anybody alive.

26
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:43,250
Then you know more than
most husbands ever do.

27
00:02:48,033 --> 00:02:53,893
I'll wear my mother's wedding
dress, so you'll see me in it first.

28
00:02:57,875 --> 00:03:03,502
A bride by mail. Like a
sack of flour from Denver.

29
00:03:03,542 --> 00:03:07,002
At least she's coming for love, Agatha.

30
00:03:07,042 --> 00:03:10,332
Caleb. The stage was hit on the pass.

31
00:03:15,185 --> 00:03:17,865
Rose! Rose Calloway!

32
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:24,159
He searched the pass all night, calling
a name he had written twenty-six times

33
00:03:24,284 --> 00:03:27,015
and never once said out loud.

34
00:03:27,419 --> 00:03:29,001
He did not find her.

35
00:03:29,404 --> 00:03:31,497
Someone else did.

36
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:37,320
Easy, miss. If I meant you
harm, you'd know it already.

37
00:03:38,798 --> 00:03:39,998
Are you one of them?

38
00:03:41,237 --> 00:03:44,077
No, ma'am. I'm the one
who found you first.

39
00:03:45,283 --> 00:03:49,943
You'll stay here. Nobody
touches a woman under my roof.

40
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:52,360
Are you the bride?

41
00:03:53,832 --> 00:03:55,152
I was supposed to be.

42
00:03:56,538 --> 00:04:00,098
Mama, is Mr. Mercer ever going to ask you?

43
00:04:01,295 --> 00:04:03,285
Eat your supper, Lily.

44
00:04:03,792 --> 00:04:08,628
It had been almost a year since a quiet
stranger named John Mercer saved Clara

45
00:04:08,668 --> 00:04:10,157
Whitmore's ranch.

46
00:04:10,468 --> 00:04:11,945
He had never left.

47
00:04:12,558 --> 00:04:16,976
Every night after supper he said good
night at the kitchen door and went out

48
00:04:17,016 --> 00:04:18,563
to sleep in the barn.

49
00:04:19,059 --> 00:04:22,104
The whole town was waiting
for him to ask her.

50
00:04:22,496 --> 00:04:26,550
That night, after Lily was
asleep, they tried the box.

51
00:04:26,791 --> 00:04:30,010
The brass key from Amos
opened the padlock.

52
00:04:30,193 --> 00:04:37,289
Inside was a second lock, a small steel
one, and no key that any of them had.

53
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:40,300
Gold would rattle.

54
00:04:41,227 --> 00:04:43,007
Then what is worth killing for?

55
00:04:44,175 --> 00:04:48,235
Five hundred dollars for the box,
Mrs. Whitmore. No questions asked.

56
00:04:50,250 --> 00:04:52,490
I haven't seen any box, Mr. Crane.

57
00:04:53,427 --> 00:04:56,567
Lovely house. So many doors.

58
00:04:57,605 --> 00:05:00,715
Mrs. Whitmore said good day, Mr. Crane.

59
00:05:01,208 --> 00:05:03,788
Mercer was not watching Crane.

60
00:05:04,192 --> 00:05:08,316
He was watching the tall roan
that Crane's man held at the gate,

61
00:05:08,395 --> 00:05:13,355
and the shoe on its left front hoof that
rang wrong on the stones of the yard.

62
00:05:13,851 --> 00:05:17,987
That night, the dog in the
yard went quiet all at once.

63
00:05:31,208 --> 00:05:32,650
The man got away.

64
00:05:32,822 --> 00:05:36,098
But as he crossed the yard,
Mercer heard it again.

65
00:05:36,491 --> 00:05:40,069
A loose shoe, ringing
on the left front hoof.

66
00:05:40,554 --> 00:05:42,693
The box was not in the barn.

67
00:05:42,922 --> 00:05:45,711
It was under a loose
board in Clara's kitchen.

68
00:05:45,883 --> 00:05:49,241
And Silas Crane had run out of patience.

69
00:05:50,670 --> 00:05:55,630
That box holds my gold, Marshal.
And that woman was in on it.

70
00:05:56,703 --> 00:06:01,303
Bring her in, Caleb. The law's the law.

71
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:04,153
She's no thief, Abel.

72
00:06:05,527 --> 00:06:07,247
Then prove it. But bring her in.

73
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:13,095
Rose had spent two days mending her
mother's wedding dress by the kitchen lamp.

74
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:16,949
She had promised him he
would see her in it first.

75
00:06:17,562 --> 00:06:19,631
He came for her that afternoon.

76
00:06:19,872 --> 00:06:21,442
With a warrant.

77
00:06:22,748 --> 00:06:24,568
Not one more step, Deputy.

78
00:06:25,810 --> 00:06:29,640
It's all right, Clara. I'll go.

79
00:06:30,055 --> 00:06:31,815
You're taller than I imagined.

80
00:06:33,207 --> 00:06:35,287
I promised you'd see me in it first.

81
00:06:36,752 --> 00:06:38,252
And you're under arrest, ma'am.

82
00:06:39,583 --> 00:06:42,140
The jail was at the
far end of Main Street.

83
00:06:42,544 --> 00:06:46,795
Caleb had to walk her past
every door in Cedar Bluff.

84
00:06:48,462 --> 00:06:53,558
Look at her, ladies. Ordered
by mail, delivered in irons.

85
00:06:54,462 --> 00:06:58,472
One more word, Agatha, and
I'll tell them about Denver.

86
00:07:06,908 --> 00:07:11,468
I wrote you every Sunday for
six months. I meant every word.

87
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,990
I didn't steal anything, Caleb.

88
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,920
I know.

89
00:07:17,917 --> 00:07:22,900
He read to her that night through the
bars, from a battered copy of Ivanhoe.

90
00:07:23,211 --> 00:07:25,942
She corrected his pronunciation twice.

91
00:07:26,346 --> 00:07:31,228
Before we go on: many of you are
listening tonight while you cook,

92
00:07:31,268 --> 00:07:34,533
or drive, or sit somewhere quiet.

93
00:07:35,030 --> 00:07:39,889
If Rose and Caleb are keeping you company,
tell me in the comments where you're

94
00:07:39,929 --> 00:07:41,081
listening from.

95
00:07:41,578 --> 00:07:43,693
I read every one.

96
00:07:44,306 --> 00:07:46,689
Now, back to the jail.

97
00:07:47,185 --> 00:07:50,160
That night was far from over.

98
00:07:51,705 --> 00:07:55,625
Why did a man who writes like
you need a matrimonial paper?

99
00:07:57,075 --> 00:08:04,295
Out here, nobody ever asked
what I was thinking. You did.

100
00:08:04,875 --> 00:08:08,024
She put her hand through
the bars, and he held it,

101
00:08:08,068 --> 00:08:09,998
and neither of them let go.

102
00:08:10,494 --> 00:08:13,991
At two in the morning,
the window exploded.

103
00:08:26,890 --> 00:08:29,540
Stay behind me, Rose!

104
00:08:34,625 --> 00:08:36,462
They wanted the box.

105
00:08:36,645 --> 00:08:38,749
It was not in the jail.

106
00:08:39,246 --> 00:08:44,186
Mercer dragged Caleb out of the smoke
and unlocked the cell with keys too hot

107
00:08:44,226 --> 00:08:49,128
to hold. By sunrise the
jail was a black shell,

108
00:08:49,254 --> 00:08:54,805
Clara had brought Rose a dress, and the
marshal released her into Clara's keeping.

109
00:08:55,116 --> 00:08:59,867
And in the ashes by the hitching
rail, Mercer found a horseshoe.

110
00:09:00,364 --> 00:09:04,221
One nail on the left side
was snapped off short.

111
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:06,940
You could have been killed.

112
00:09:08,558 --> 00:09:11,158
I wrote you I'd look
after you. Meant that too.

113
00:09:12,242 --> 00:09:20,085
Broken nail, left fore. That
horse stood at Clara's gate.

114
00:09:20,702 --> 00:09:22,202
Buck Tolliver's roan.

115
00:09:23,417 --> 00:09:28,644
But a horseshoe was not proof against
the most respected man in the valley.

116
00:09:29,141 --> 00:09:31,593
They needed what was in the box.

117
00:09:32,090 --> 00:09:36,481
That night, Rose Calloway
asked Clara for a hairpin.

118
00:09:37,528 --> 00:09:43,298
My father printed handbills for
every locksmith in St. Louis.

119
00:09:43,882 --> 00:09:46,342
Every gold shipment date. For two years.

120
00:09:47,743 --> 00:09:49,863
Unsigned letters prove nothing.

121
00:09:51,403 --> 00:09:56,833
A man can change his name.
He can't change his hand.

122
00:09:57,333 --> 00:09:59,727
The same hand had written both.

123
00:10:00,131 --> 00:10:04,963
Silas Crane had signed his own
confession and handed it to the law.

124
00:10:05,274 --> 00:10:09,027
A frightened clerk in Denver had
been selling him the gold schedule.

125
00:10:09,268 --> 00:10:14,093
When the clerk lost his nerve, he gave
Crane's letters to the only honest man

126
00:10:14,133 --> 00:10:17,003
he knew. Amos Pruitt.

127
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:20,567
There had never been any gold in that box.

128
00:10:20,878 --> 00:10:25,772
Crane had invented it, so the bride would
hang before anyone read what she was

129
00:10:25,812 --> 00:10:27,394
carrying.

130
00:10:28,875 --> 00:10:30,195
Why do you stay, John?

131
00:10:31,837 --> 00:10:33,037
You know why.

132
00:10:34,208 --> 00:10:37,531
At dawn the marshal
rode out with a warrant.

133
00:10:37,842 --> 00:10:41,107
Crane's house was empty
and the safe stood open.

134
00:10:41,511 --> 00:10:44,126
Mercer read the ground
for less than a minute.

135
00:10:44,529 --> 00:10:46,517
Red Canyon, he said.

136
00:10:47,014 --> 00:10:49,339
Caleb rode with his arm in a sling.

137
00:10:49,743 --> 00:10:52,288
Nobody could talk him out of it.

138
00:11:05,542 --> 00:11:07,704
Buck Tolliver had the high ground.

139
00:11:07,887 --> 00:11:11,965
But the war had taught John
Mercer one thing above all others.

140
00:11:12,369 --> 00:11:13,776
You don't go up.

141
00:11:14,087 --> 00:11:16,191
You go around.

142
00:11:23,177 --> 00:11:24,377
Where's Crane?

143
00:11:25,633 --> 00:11:27,953
Ask the bride.

144
00:11:29,208 --> 00:11:31,126
The canyon was a decoy.

145
00:11:31,623 --> 00:11:36,386
Crane had gone back to Cedar Bluff
for the one thing he still needed.

146
00:11:36,882 --> 00:11:39,311
Clara had taken Lily into town.

147
00:11:39,715 --> 00:11:42,783
Rose was alone in the kitchen.

148
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:49,580
The box, Miss Calloway. And
then we'll take a little ride.

149
00:12:02,745 --> 00:12:03,945
Let her go, Crane.

150
00:12:05,547 --> 00:12:08,147
With one arm, Deputy? Step aside.

151
00:12:18,958 --> 00:12:23,448
Silas Crane. You're under
arrest for robbing the mail.

152
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:28,456
Silas Crane had spent his whole
life underestimating people.

153
00:12:28,953 --> 00:12:31,115
Ranchers. Old guards.

154
00:12:31,194 --> 00:12:32,601
Shy deputies.

155
00:12:32,784 --> 00:12:34,853
And a bride who came by mail.

156
00:12:35,257 --> 00:12:38,290
Amos Pruitt lived to testify in Denver.

157
00:12:38,775 --> 00:12:42,725
Crane and Buck Tolliver went to
the penitentiary at Cañon City.

158
00:12:43,035 --> 00:12:46,916
And a week later, on the same street
where the town had laughed at her,

159
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:50,120
Caleb Ward got down on one knee.

160
00:12:51,055 --> 00:12:56,415
Rose Calloway. Will you marry
me? Properly, this time.

161
00:12:57,195 --> 00:13:00,905
I came a thousand miles to say yes.

162
00:13:01,637 --> 00:13:04,877
Miss Calloway. I was mistaken.

163
00:13:04,917 --> 00:13:08,217
Then come to the wedding, Mrs. Pell.

164
00:13:08,708 --> 00:13:11,927
But the best moment of that
day happened at sunset,

165
00:13:12,168 --> 00:13:15,085
and almost nobody saw it.

166
00:13:16,463 --> 00:13:20,163
Clara, I reckon I've slept
in that barn long enough.

167
00:13:21,542 --> 00:13:24,052
About time, John Mercer.

168
00:13:24,542 --> 00:13:28,608
They were married in October,
when the aspens turned gold.

169
00:13:28,977 --> 00:13:34,332
Caleb and Rose stood up for them, and
the next spring it was their turn.

170
00:13:34,794 --> 00:13:37,722
Would you have stood up
for Rose on that street,

171
00:13:38,010 --> 00:13:41,181
or stayed quiet like the rest of the town?

172
00:13:41,678 --> 00:13:43,643
Tell me in the comments.

173
00:13:43,826 --> 00:13:49,192
And subscribe, because there are
more stories waiting in Cedar Bluff.

174
00:13:49,596 --> 00:13:53,534
Until next time, keep
a light in the window.

